# Content-Security-Policy applied to index.html via the %VITE_CSP% placeholder.
# This file is the shared baseline; `.env.development` relaxes it for Vite's dev
# server (inline React-refresh preamble, injected <style> tags, loopback HMR
# websocket) and `.env.production` keeps the locked-down policy that ships.
#
# `ipc:` / `http://ipc.localhost` are Tauri v2's IPC origins (the latter on
# Windows and Android) and must stay in connect-src or `invoke()` is blocked.
# `frame-ancestors` is intentionally absent here: browsers ignore it when the
# policy arrives via <meta>. It lives in `app.security.csp` in tauri.conf.json,
# which Tauri serves as a real Content-Security-Policy header where it applies.
#
# Fonts are fully vendored locally in public/fonts/ (Geist and JetBrains Mono);
# no remote origins permitted.
VITE_CSP=default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' ipc: http://ipc.localhost; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-src 'none'; form-action 'none'
